Handwritten Text Recognition (HTR) in diverse languages remains a complex task due to varying alphabets and limited availability of labeled data. To overcome this challenge, a novel approach is presented that generates labeled characters from unlabeled documents in a single step. The proposed method utilizes a trained deep learning model to produce character-level annotations directly from input documents without requiring segmentation into words or lines. To prevent overfitting, a line detection module is included to filter documents that defy this segmentation process. The method's efficacy is demonstrated on two languages with complex alphabets - Tamil and Gujarati - with positive results. The source code for this research can be accessed at https://github.com/ankitkumar123/Single-shot-HCR. 

